title: Bucket — a state-driven line (ADR-366 D5a)
story: vehicles
description: The bucket is a line whose position block answers from what it
  holds. Fill it and it rises with the player aboard; empty it and it falls.
  The machine reports the arrival to the rider; a turn with no change moves
  nothing.

---

> take water
[OK: contains "Taken"]

> enter bucket
[OK: contains "get into the bucket"]

# Fill: the position block now answers the Top of the Well
> put water in bucket
[OK: contains "The bucket arrives at the Top of the Well."]

> look
[OK: contains "Top of the Well"]

# Nothing changed: nothing moves
> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

# Empty: the position block answers the Well Bottom again
> take water
[OK: contains "The bucket arrives at the Well Bottom."]

> look
[OK: contains "Well Bottom"]

> exit
[OK: contains "You get out of the bucket."]
